# Response headers of the site on Cloudflare (Workers static assets).
#
# Cloudflare sends every file with "Cache-Control: public, max-age=0,
# must-revalidate" and an ETag: browsers check pages and unhashed files
# (HTML, pagefind.js, pagefind-entry.json, wasm.*.pagefind, og.png, llms.txt)
# each time, and get a 304 when they did not change. Only files whose name
# carries a hash of their content are cached for a year, below.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy yet: the theme script and the structured data
# are inline and Pagefind compiles WebAssembly, so a policy needs their hashes
# (or 'unsafe-inline') and 'wasm-unsafe-eval', and a check that search still
# works. Neither X-Frame-Options nor frame-ancestors: the dashboard of every
# Spawner server, on whatever domain it runs, opens these docs in an iframe,
# and the site has no account, form or action a framing page could misuse.
# HSTS without includeSubDomains or preload until every subdomain of
# spawner.run is served over HTTPS.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/fragment/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/index/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/filter/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/*.pf_meta
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The Markdown copy of a page tells search engines that the page is the original.
/docs/:page.md
  Link: <https://spawner.run/docs/:page/>; rel="canonical"

/changelog.md
  Link: <https://spawner.run/changelog/>; rel="canonical"
